---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadMeta } from "../../lib/catalog.js";
import { formatDate, formatNumber } from "../../lib/format.js";

const meta = loadMeta();
---

<Base
  title="Guides"
  description="Short explanations of technical service bulletins, whether a recall expires, what an open recall means, and how long a recall remedy lasts, with the government source named."
  canonicalPath="/guides/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }]}
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Guides</h1>
    <div class="answer">
      <p>
        These notes use NHTSA's published descriptions and the recall file dated {formatDate(meta.dates.recalls)}, which lists {formatNumber(meta.counts.vehicleCampaignsPost2010)} vehicle campaigns from 2010 on and {formatNumber(meta.counts.vehicleCampaignsPre2010)} in the older file. This site has not imported manufacturer communications.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/guides/what-is-a-tsb/">What is a TSB</a></li>
      <li><a href="/guides/do-recalls-expire/">Do recalls expire</a></li>
      <li><a href="/guides/open-recall-meaning/">What an open recall means</a></li>
      <li><a href="/guides/how-long-do-recalls-last/">How long recalls last</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
